ConnectivityService: Keep auto-join for a network without Internet access

When a network the user picked failed validation, handlePromptUnvalidated()
told its transport never to reconnect to it automatically. Wi-Fi turns
that into NETWORK_SELECTION_DISABLED_NO_INTERNET_PERMANENT, saved with the
network. An Echo on a network without Internet access, such as a VLAN
that only reaches Home Assistant, stayed connected until the next reboot
or drop and then never rejoined, since it has no screen or nobody at it
to turn auto-join back on. Keep the prompt, but not the disable.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java
index 6a34fc73..d604609b 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java
@@ -4196,11 +4196,9 @@ public class ConnectivityService extends IConnectivityManager.Stub
             return;
         }
 
-        // Stop automatically reconnecting to this network in the future. Automatically connecting
-        // to a network that provides no or limited connectivity is not useful, because the user
-        // cannot use that network except through the notification shown by this method, and the
-        // notification is only shown if the network is explicitly selected by the user.
-        nai.asyncChannel.sendMessage(NetworkAgent.CMD_PREVENT_AUTOMATIC_RECONNECT);
+        // Kiosk Satellite Edition: keep reconnecting to it. An Echo on a network without Internet
+        // access, such as a VLAN that only reaches Home Assistant, still does all its work there.
+        // It has no screen or nobody at it to turn auto-join back on.
 
